                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "71ca7404-42a6-3b46-8789-f14789e02a23",
                                        "entry_id": "0664fa2d-fb92-3e37-a7b3-1abf987ba583",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A woody plant distinguished from a tree by its multiple stems and lower height, being usually less than six metres tall; a horticultural rather than strictly botanical category."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "adbdaf29-996d-4aae-ad08-f67f415f59b0",
                                                "sense_id": "71ca7404-42a6-3b46-8789-f14789e02a23",
                                                "text": "I stumbled along through the young pines and huckleberry bushes. Pretty soon I struck into a sort of path that, I cal'lated, might lead to the road I was hunting for. It twisted and turned, and, the first thing I knew, made a sudden bend around a bunch of bayberry scrub and opened out into a big clear space like a lawn."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e6b4e642-7a54-38de-a78c-cd3df7997231",
                                        "entry_id": "0664fa2d-fb92-3e37-a7b3-1abf987ba583",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A shrub cut off, or a shrublike branch of a tree."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b162af8d-46aa-4453-a756-d7725c8d0da8",
                                                "sense_id": "e6b4e642-7a54-38de-a78c-cd3df7997231",
                                                "text": "bushes to support pea vines"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7638f1b3-9ecf-339a-87a3-b04aad14d197",
                                        "entry_id": "0664fa2d-fb92-3e37-a7b3-1abf987ba583",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A shrub or branch, properly, a branch of ivy (sacred to Bacchus), hung out at vintners' doors, or as a tavern sign; hence, a tavern sign, and symbolically, the tavern itself."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c53424e-7850-4bcb-9867-72cecc28135e",
                                                "sense_id": "7638f1b3-9ecf-339a-87a3-b04aad14d197",
                                                "text": "If it be true, that good wine needs no buſh, 'tis true, that a good play needes no Epilogue."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d726287e-67be-4dd2-9ec2-c201b1380487",
                                                "sense_id": "7638f1b3-9ecf-339a-87a3-b04aad14d197",
                                                "text": "\"Well,\" replied Lady Mary, \"who is to know where good wine is sold, unless you hang out the bush.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2a7d3ed6-7786-3696-b206-3c1f62248720",
                                        "entry_id": "0664fa2d-fb92-3e37-a7b3-1abf987ba583",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person's pubic hair, especially a woman's."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang",
                                            "vulgar"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c64acdb-f047-4afd-9714-20c4184573bd",
                                                "sense_id": "2a7d3ed6-7786-3696-b206-3c1f62248720",
                                                "text": "As he ſtood on one ſide for a minute or ſo, unbuttoning his waſte-coat, and breeches, her fat brawny thighs hung down, and the whole greaſy landſkip lay fairly open to my view: a wide open-mouth’d gap, overſhaded with a grizzly buſh, ſeemed held out like a beggar’s wallet for its’ proviſion.",
                                                "translation": "Fanny Hill",
                                                "english": "Fanny Hill"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "befaeb92-d624-42a2-8507-e8fc566d5498",
                                                "sense_id": "2a7d3ed6-7786-3696-b206-3c1f62248720",
                                                "text": "I rub her bush with my cheek and my chin, tickle her bonne-bouche with my tongue."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e40a0af-caf9-44d1-9783-f199101074bd",
                                                "sense_id": "2a7d3ed6-7786-3696-b206-3c1f62248720",
                                                "text": "But no, the little pool of semen was there, proof positive, with droplets caught hanging in her bush."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8d1489e-33d7-4fb9-8600-c6c6a02d9bef",
                                                "sense_id": "2a7d3ed6-7786-3696-b206-3c1f62248720",
                                                "text": "I push my seed in her bush for life / It's gonna work because I'm pushing it right"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2f2d3f47-7515-4a9a-a801-64c41b0783d6",
                                                "sense_id": "2a7d3ed6-7786-3696-b206-3c1f62248720",
                                                "text": "I think on Saturday I'm gonna find out if red-haired girls have a red bush!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aade8fa6-cda9-33d2-9b05-dd4dbc16ed0f",
